1654	/// Read all entries from a single WAL file.
1655	///
1656	/// RC4 W1 #8: checkpoint-based skipping is GONE from replay (see
1657	/// `WalReader::replay` docs).  The 2026-07 S3 "offset-bounded skip"
1658	/// hardening was the previous, weaker containment of the same bug class
1659	/// (stale/over-broad checkpoints discarding acked entries); removing the
1660	/// skip entirely is its logical conclusion — replay-side loss is now
1661	/// structurally impossible, and dedup of already-flushed entries is the
1662	/// job of the idempotent replay consumers.
1663	///
1664	/// RC4 W2 #13 — BOUNDARY RESYNC: a corrupt region no longer aborts the
1665	/// whole file.  Pre-fix the parser `break`-ed at the first bad frame, so
1666	/// a mid-file tear (crash/ENOSPC leftover appended over by a pre-fix
1667	/// binary, or disk rot) silently dropped every acked entry after it
